{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"Local profiling shows the safe fusion saves about 0.04–0.07 ms per call, while changing the skip convolution to a linear layer loses that gain once its output layout is converted. I’m reverting that path and instead fusing the initial sequence-to-spatial transpose, group normalization, and SiLU; this attacks roughly 0.4 ms on a mid-sized workload while keeping the tuned convolutions intact."}}
